@@ -1,9 +1,9 @@
-IDS_ABOUT_ABOUT_TEXTss=\nWinDirStat - Directory Statistics\n\n"Shows where all your drive space has gone\nand helps you clean it up."\n\nProgrammed for Microsoft Windows by\nBernhard Seifert, Oliver Schneider, Bryan Berns\n(mailto:{}),\n\nBased on Stefan Hundhammer's KDE (Linux) application KDirStat\n(https://kdirstat.sourceforge.net/).\n\nWinDirStat's home is {}/\n\nCopyright © WinDirStat Team
+IDS_ABOUT_ABOUT_TEXTss=\nSoul Disk Map — based on WinDirStat\n\nWinDirStat - Directory Statistics\n\n"Shows where all your drive space has gone\nand helps you clean it up."\n\nProgrammed for Microsoft Windows by\nBernhard Seifert, Oliver Schneider, Bryan Berns\n(mailto:{}),\n\nBased on Stefan Hundhammer's KDE (Linux) application KDirStat\n(https://kdirstat.sourceforge.net/).\n\nWinDirStat's home is {}/\n\nCopyright © WinDirStat Team
 IDS_ABOUT_ABOUT=About
 IDS_ABOUT_LICENSE=License
 IDS_ABOUT_THANKS_TEXT=\nStefan Hundhammer for his superb Linux tool KDirStat.\nUsing KDirStat (2.3.7) as a specification saved me a lot of time.\nhttps://kdirstat.sourceforge.net/\n\nThe authors of SequoiaView for showing just how useful treemaps really can be.\nhttps://www.win.tue.nl/sequoiaview/\n\nJarke J. van Wijk, Huub van de Wetering, Mark Bruls and Kees Huizing\nfor their papers about cushion treemaps and squarified treemaps.\nhttps://www.win.tue.nl/~vanwijk/\n\nBen Shneiderman for his ingenious idea of treemaps -\na truly intuitive way of visualizing tree contents.\nhttps://www.cs.umd.edu/hcil/TreeMap.history/\n
 IDS_ABOUT_THANKS=Thanks To
-IDS_ABOUT_TITLE=About WinDirStat
+IDS_ABOUT_TITLE=About Soul Disk Map
 IDS_ADMIN=Administrator
 IDS_ALL_FILES=All Files
 IDS_ANALYTICS_CONFIG=Parameters
